  "scenario": "Equal point allowances; legal paid edits to intended archetypes; levels 2/7/13 at floors 2/5/10. Injury-throughput probe resets wounds before each of 18 rolls against a harmless, three-roll-frequency dummy. Separate fresh real staircase guardian trials use unchanged actor selection, no gear, items, lessons, rare luck saves or travel. Fixed stages are not campaign outcomes; some builds leave points unspent because the next purchase is unaffordable.",
  "limitations": [
    "No campaign win-rate estimate; fixed isolated stages and no purchased camp lessons.",
    "Healed HP is gross throughput; net subtracts actual Seed offerings. Wounds reset each roll only in the recovery probe.",
    "Builds retain the best forecast among affordable matching-column upgrade steps; they are not globally optimised.",
    "Some point budgets remain unspent to preserve matching ranks.",
    "Early defensive Bloodbinder starts with more heal faces than Mage; at the tiny 8-point allowance it can heal more despite weaker late recovery.",
    "The high-HP recovery dummy excludes Exchange from direct-damage totals. Guardians are separate actual fights."
